R-AL2 R-RG1 R-RG2 R-RG7 R-FL5 R-RG4 R-DI1 R-AP16 R-AP74 R-DI14 R-AL8 R-DT3 R-DT5 R-AP19 R-J3 R-EC2 R-IX3 (slice 206b): `tln update` reaches a registry (entry `commands`, the whole command code). The registry is http://127.0.0.1:9 in config.toml (R-RG1 source 3); the answer is fx/http/<host>/v1/closure.POST (no-store; the route requires content-type and no Authorization). The given home keeps the public answers of acme/json and acme/pfx (R-RG5); acme/parser is not kept. All runs use --no-check (no probe), so the facts of the tuple come only from the index.
Run 1: `--registry direct` wins over TALON_REGISTRY and config.toml (R-RG1): the direct calls of before the slice (GitHub release lists, the archives read for the closure), the line `resolved at <time>` (R-DT5 direct).
Run 2: config.toml gives the registry. After the load (one read of the project files and config.toml), the guard reads the 3 kept answers in one call and asks GitHub only for acme/parser, then writes its answer (R-RG4, R-RG5), BEFORE the one POST /v1/closure (R-AL2 step 2). Body (R-AP16, R-DI1, R-AP74 rows 3 and 5): the free variables of `update` (all) in priority order with series and the implied range, the hashes of the header in header order, the window of the held pin. `--snapshot log:30` hides the releases above 30 except the header hashes (R-AP19, Q403): json moves to 2.1.0 (log 25), parser stays at 1.0.0, pf stays at 0.1.0 (0.1.1 is log 33). No GitHub list, no archive read (R-DI14, R-AL8 source 2). `--json`: `"snapshot":"log:30"` (R-DT5, R-J3), the human lines on stderr. Dry run: no header write.
Run 3: a bad TALON_REGISTRY wins over config.toml: exit 2, the message names the source and the text (R-RG7 row 6, R-EC2), after the load, no guard, no request. Run 4: the same for `--registry http://example.org` (http only to a loopback host, R-RG7 row 1).
Run 5: TALON_REGISTRY `HTTP://LocalHost:9/` wins over config.toml and is read in the base URL form http://localhost:9 (R-RG7 rows 2, 3): the POST goes to that origin. The guard reads the 3 kept answers (acme/parser was kept in run 2) and sends no request. The answer gives json 2.1.0 (2.2.0 is younger than min-release-age), parser 1.2.0 (1.3.0 is withdrawn), pf 0.1.1; the header is written; `resolved at log:50, 0 probes` (the log_size of the answer, R-DT5). No file of the answer is kept (R-IX3).
Slice 206d2 (Design Q438, a proposal R-OUT2): the --json run 2 has `"log_size":30` after `"snapshot":"log:30"` (the R-DT5 number).
